// Import necessary libraries
import java.io.IOException;
import java.net.URI;
import java.util.HashMap;
import java.util.Map;

import javax.websocket.OnClose;
import javax.websocket.OnError;
import javax.websocket.OnMessage;
import javax.websocket.OnOpen;
import javax.websocket.Session;
import javax.websocket.server.ServerEndpoint;

@ServerEndpoint("/chat")
public class ChatServer {

    // Map to hold active sessions
    private static Map<Session, String> sessions = new HashMap<>();

    @OnOpen
    public void onOpen(Session session) {
        sessions.put(session, "connected");
        System.out.println("New client connected: " + session.getId());
    }

    @OnMessage
    public void onMessage(String message, Session session) throws IOException {
        // Broadcast message to all clients or handle based on protocol
        for (Session s : sessions.keySet()) {
            if (!s.getId().equals(session.getId())) {
                s.getBasicRemote().sendText(message);
            }
        }
    }

    @OnClose
    public void onClose(Session session) {
        sessions.remove(session);
        System.out.println("Client disconnected: " + session.getId());
    }

    @OnError
    public void onError(Session session, Throwable throwable) {
        // Log or handle errors
        System.err.println("Error occurred with client " + session.getId() + ": " + throwable.getMessage());
    }
}
```

This code snippet provides a basic framework for a WebSocket server in Java using the `javax.websocket` API. It includes methods to handle connections, messages, and disconnections. The server maintains a map of active sessions to manage client connections dynamically.

For a more comprehensive solution, additional components would be required, such as handling different messaging protocols, implementing message queuing with libraries like Apache Kafka or RabbitMQ, integrating with an external notification service, ensuring scalability through load balancing and efficient use of resources, and developing a robust error handling and logging system.

